  "type": "Definition",
  "number": "1.4.14",
  "title": "Linear Equation and Linear Inequality.",
  "body": " Linear Equation and Linear Inequality   A linear equation in one variable is any equation where one side is a linear Linear equations expression in that variable, and the other side is either a constant number, or is another Equation linear linear expression in that variable. A linear inequality in one variable is Linear equations in one variable defined similarly, just with an inequality symbol instead of an equal sign. Linear inequalities  Inequality linear  Linear inequalities in one variable    "
